      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-240417",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the independent random variables $Y_{1}\u223c\u0393(2, 3)$ and $Y_{2}\u223cExp(3)$. What is the distribution of $Y = Y_{1} + Y_{2}$?\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following results.*\n\n| Distribution | $M(t)$ | $t$-domain |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $U[a, b]$ | ${(e^{tb} - e^{ta})/(t(b - a)),\\begin{vmatrix}t \\ne 0 \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}t = 0$ | $t \u2208 R$ |\n| $N(\u03bc, \u03c3^{2})$ | $\\exp (\u03bct + \\frac{1}{2}\u03c3^{2}t^{2})$ | $t \u2208 R$ |\n| $\u03c7^{2}(k)$ | $(1 - 2t)^{-k/2}$ | $t < \\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $Exp(\u03bb)$ | $\\frac{\u03bb}{\u03bb - t}$ | $t < \u03bb$ |\n| $\u0393(\u03b1, \u03bb)$ | $(\\frac{\u03bb}{\u03bb - t})^{\u03b1}$ | $t < \u03bb$ |"
    },
